      "text": "Okay, so day two, we're back into Swift AI, and, you know, you just... it opens right up to goal, which is fine. It shows you what your goal is, and then, you know, what it's prescribing you for each of the categories: activity and personal training, nutrition, mind and wellness. And then today it lists the things, you know. It has your strength plan, which is upper body strength, and then your water goals, food goals, which, yeah, it's all fine, post-workout stretch, warm-up mobility, those are all fine. So I hit the start button on the upper body strength, and it immediately takes me to the log, which is good, but it puts me in a search bar and the keyboard comes up, and so I don't know why it would do that. It lists dumbbell row, goblet squat, which is not upper body, dumbbell Romanian deadlifts, dumbbell overhead press. So those are the four, and it says 4x6, 4x6, 4x6, 3x8, is the rep schemes for those four lifts. So half of them are not even upper body, and they only show one field for sets, one field for reps, one field for the pounds, and there's a checkbox next to the name. And those four are checked. Below it are four more lifts that are not checked. And it's easy bar curl, leg press, seated Russian twists, snatch grip deadlift. So some of these, I mean, they're not upper body. And it says duration, 45 minutes, here's some notes, and then it gives you a place to select the RPE, the rate of perceived exertion, for the overall lift. And then you just hit log workout. So right off the bat, if this is the workout that it's prescribing to you, it's wrong. It's not what it says it's going to be because it's not upper body. Yeah, I mean, the rep schemes are okay, but, you know, for strength work, I guess. But there's no per set logging, no rest timer. Yeah, it feels, it feels very thin, I would say.\n",
